# data-pipeline/.env.example
# Copy this file to data-pipeline/.env (that file is git-ignored) and fill it in ON YOUR OWN COMPUTER ONLY.
# Never paste these values into a chat, an issue, a commit or any frontend code.
#
# You only need credentials for datasets that require an Earthdata Login (currently: sea-level GMSL from PO.DAAC).
# Public sources (NASA SVS, GISTEMP, NSIDC Sea Ice Index, CMR search) need NO login and ignore this file.
#
# OPTION A (recommended): an Earthdata user token. It can be revoked and it expires, and it does not expose your password.
# Generate it while signed in at https://urs.earthdata.nasa.gov (follow the on-screen token page).
EARTHDATA_TOKEN=
#
# OPTION B: username and password. Less safe than a token. Leave blank if you use Option A or a _netrc file.
EARTHDATA_USERNAME=
EARTHDATA_PASSWORD=
#
# OPTION C: no .env at all. Run  python data-pipeline/scripts/earthdata_auth.py --setup-interactive
# and type your password into the hidden prompt. earthaccess then stores it in your user folder (outside this repository).
